      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wilcoxne.com/our-community/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Bank of Wilcox opened in June 1886 with $10,000 capital, marking the town’s first financial institution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wilcoxne.com/our-community/history/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Wilcox’s early businesses included a general store, hardware, furniture, drug store, lumber companies, and a newspaper called the Wilcox Beacon.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wilcoxne.com/our-community/history/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first settler, Charles Walker, established Walker’s Ranch in 1872 as a station on the government mail route.",
